################################################################################
# fpga/targets/kr260-eth-chiplet/board_glue.flist  --  RTL_FLIST for this target
#
# WHAT THIS FLIST IS FOR, WHICH IS NOT WHAT A FLIST IS USUALLY FOR
# ===========================================================================
# On this target the SoC does not arrive as RTL.  It arrives as the PACKAGED IP
# `soclabs.org:user:nanosoc_eth_chiplet_vivado_wrapper:1.0`, instantiated by the
# block design, resolved through IP_REPOS.  So the RTL this flow COMPILES is
# only the glue between that IP and the board - and that is what this file
# lists.
#
# It lists ONE file: the PHY link/pad clock /2 divider.  The block design
# instantiates it BY MODULE REFERENCE
# (`create_bd_cell -type module -reference tidelink_phy_clk_div2`), and a module
# reference resolves only against a file already in sources_1.  The flist stage
# is what puts it there, before the bd stage runs.
#
# The other loose file - the board-level top, tidelink_design_wrapper.v, which
# carries the SWDIO and MDIO IOBUFs - is named by TOP_HDL and read after the
# flist by the synth stage.  It is deliberately NOT here: a file in both places
# is read twice and elaborates as a duplicate module definition.
#
# TOGETHER THOSE TWO ARE EXACTLY THE LEGACY FLOW'S FILESET, and that is the
# point.  Measured on the shipping build's own project file:
#
#     $ grep -oE '<File Path="[^"]*"' tidelink_project.xpr | grep -cE '\.(v|sv|svh)$'
#     2
#         tidelink_design_wrapper.v
#         tidelink_phy_clk_div2.v
#
#
# WHAT THIS FLIST IS NOT
# ===========================================================================
# It is NOT the SoC's flist.  flist/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.flist - 596 sources - is
# what BUILDS the packaged IP, and it belongs to the packaging step
# (PACKAGE_TCL, stage 2), which this project does not yet run.  Pointing
# RTL_FLIST at it while also consuming the prebuilt IP put every SoC module into
# the build TWICE: once loose, once inside the IP.  See design.mk section 5.
#
# Copyright (C) 2026, SoC Labs (www.soclabs.org)
################################################################################

../../../tidelink/fpga/targets/kr260-eth-chiplet/tidelink_phy_clk_div2.v
